WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
[Screen reader voice synthesizes text] Web Accessibility Perspectives: Text to Speech. Many computers and mobile devices today have built-in text-to-speech software.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:14.000
It's technology that many people who are blind have been relying on for years, and it's also important for many people with dyslexia.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:22.500
[Page turns, tablet speaks article aloud] And it's very useful for people who have difficulty reading text, as well as people who like to multi-task.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:31.000
But for this to work, websites and apps have to be properly coded—which has the added benefit of helping search engines index website contents better.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:40.000
[Closing chime] Web accessibility: Essential for some, useful for all. Visit w3.org/WAI/perspectives for more information on Text to Speech.
